  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and Innovation for Global Health Transformation - Preventing Deaths from Acute Poisoning in Low and Middle Income Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A UK and low-and-middle-income-country (LMIC) research partnership that aims to prevent deaths from acute poisoning</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In LMIC engage with and involve collaborator from inception to delivery completion, design/authorship, and dissemination of project outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WP1 Methanol Poisoning; WP2 Occupational Pesticide Poisoning; WP3 Guidelines in collaboration with WHO; WP4 Increase Research Capacity. WP5 Expand Poison Information Centre Capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
